{
  "level_shipped": "L2",
  "level_name": "Hard floor",
  "shipping_reason": "Hard floor, with one constant per calendar month. Passes every check the shipping rule names, as first written: C0, C1 (-0.020), C1b, C2 (-0.059) and C3 (0.148 against 0.15, narrowly); also C3r and C4. Fails C3x, added after results: the same statistic on 2020 to 2021 is 0.169. The detection curve fails C3 (0.208) and C8 (its midpoint is too uncertain), which is why it does not ship. Until 15 Nov the hard floor with one year-round constant shipped; it failed C3 (0.169) because its error followed the season.",
  "unit": "Aqua-equivalent fire cells",
  "unit_note": "One fire cell is a 1 km square (0.01 degree) with fire in one satellite pass. Before February 2012: what Aqua MODIS reported. From February 2012: what Aqua would have reported, computed from VIIRS with the hard floor (only fire cells at or above a measured strength cut-off are counted), scaled by a constant fitted for each calendar month because the two sensors' relation follows the season.",
